@namespace NoBorders.Components.Screens
@* Monitor card, screen 1e — three visual variants (selected-connected,
   connected, saved-but-disconnected/removable).

   Phase 4.10: the card body is clickable (selects this monitor as the
   Settings > Monitors baseline-default target); Saved cards' "✕" removes
   it — @onclick:stopPropagation keeps that click from also selecting the
   card it sits on.

   review.md §4.3: "✕" was a plain <div>, not in the keyboard tab order
   and with no accessible name at all (not even a title). Now a real
   <button> with aria-label="Remove {Name}" — the card body itself stays a
   div, since its visible Name/Detail text already gives it an accessible
   name the "✕" glyph alone never had.

   Phase 8.14 (user request): a small green dot flags whichever connected
   monitor Windows currently reports as primary (State.Monitors' own
   Primary flag — same fact MainForm.GetPrimaryMonitorId already uses
   elsewhere, not recomputed here) — "primary" is a live-OS concept, so
   this only ever applies to connected cards; a Saved (disconnected) card
   never gets one even if it happens to share a name with what used to be
   the primary monitor. Reuses --nb-success, the same green already used
   for "CONNECTED" and the borderless-applied status dot, per the ask to
   match the app's existing color scheme rather than introduce a new
   green. Revised per feedback: originally an absolutely-positioned badge
   straddling the card's left border; now sized to the name's own font
   (1em, so it tracks --nb-monitor-card__name's 12.5px exactly) and sits
   inline just before the name, inside the card. *@

<div class="nb-monitor-card @VariantClass" @onclick="OnCardClick">
    <div class="nb-monitor-card__body">
        <div class="nb-monitor-card__name-row">
            @if (Primary)
            {
                <span class="nb-monitor-card__primary-dot" title="Primary monitor"></span>
            }
            <span class="nb-monitor-card__name">@Name</span>
        </div>
        <div class="nb-monitor-card__detail nb-mono">@Detail</div>
    </div>
    @if (Saved)
    {
        <button type="button" class="nb-monitor-card__remove" aria-label="Remove @Name" @onclick="OnRemoveClick" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">✕</button>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter] public string Detail { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter] public bool Selected { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool Saved { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool Primary { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnSelect { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnRemove { get; set; }

    // Bugfix: Saved short-circuited before Selected was ever checked, so a
    // disconnected card never showed any selected highlight at all —
    // clicking it visually did nothing even though State.
    // ActiveMonitorDefaultScope genuinely changed underneath it. Saved and
    // Selected are independent facts (a card can be both), so both classes
    // apply together; MonitorCard.razor.css's combined selector dials the
    // highlight down for the saved case rather than reusing the full
    // connected--selected treatment verbatim.
    private string VariantClass =>
        (Saved ? "nb-monitor-card--saved " : "") +
        (Saved && Selected ? "nb-monitor-card--saved-selected" : !Saved && Selected ? "nb-monitor-card--selected" : "");

    private Task OnCardClick() => OnSelect.InvokeAsync();
    private Task OnRemoveClick() => OnRemove.InvokeAsync();
}
